<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114401" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορδ-αψός</span></b> , ὁ (on the
		accent v. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			1.227
		</span></i>), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a disease in the
				great guts,</i> the same as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰλεός</span> in the small ones, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Coac.</u>
				502
			</span></i>; but the meanings are reversed by <i><span class="en">
				Diocl.
			</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				73
			</span></i>) ap.<i><span class="en">
				Cels.
				4.20.1
			</span></i>; an aggravated form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰλεός</span> acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SA</u>
				2.6
			</span></i>, but not distd. fr. it by <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				8.388
			</span></i> (fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορδή, ἕψω,</span> acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
			</span></i> l. c.).</div>
